ype="html">A Ukrainian woman who fled the war in her country built a lifeline for refugees in Poland. Now her organization faces donor fatigue, funding cuts and rising hostility as support for Ukrainians in Poland wanes.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>India's 'cockroaches' vs Election Commission: What you need to know ahead of CJP's October 10 protests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:432481e811e726f68a6f09055442993573896e5d6354ff9363d33b976cdd37ee</id><updated>2026-10-09T15:23:50Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T12:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-s-cockroaches-vs-election-commission-what-you-need-to-know-ahead-of-cjp-s-october-10-protests/a-79608760--fa9a4a7bb711.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-s-cockroaches-vs-election-commission-what-you-need-to-know-ahead-of-cjp-s-october-10-protests/a-79608760?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Indian capital New Delhi has been turned into a fortress with train and metro cancelations, barricades and heavy police presence ahead of Saturday's planned protests against the chief of India's electoral body.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Bosnia and Herzegovina will soon have a new Grand Mufti</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e9630b5922b37ee35fb4006253470cc4c14356d5a5cefdeb5e0a6af8275f0e2d</id><updated>2026-10-09T15:24:07Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T08:20:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/bosnia-and-herzegovina-will-soon-have-a-new-grand-mufti/a-79604402--960d4eb80e56.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/bosnia-and-herzegovina-will-soon-have-a-new-grand-mufti/a-79604402?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The new leader of the Islamic Community in Bosnia and Herzegovina will be elected on October 10. The reis-ul-ulema's role is not only important for Muslims in the country itself, but could inspire Muslims across Europe.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Finland, the world's happiest nation, faces a glum winter</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7e34aef458ccdd5e44f219baff7676bed2b510a5e24bbd635b6379a69798b71f</id><updated>2026-10-09T15:24:10Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T08:12:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/finland-the-world-s-happiest-nation-faces-a-glum-winter/a-79544348--0df829428818.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/finland-the-world-s-happiest-nation-faces-a-glum-winter/a-79544348?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Finns have many reasons to feel content, but the country's pile of debt is not one of them. Russia's war in Ukraine has added to the fiscal burden. Can the Nordic nation absorb another shock?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>EU pulls sponsorship from Disinfo2026 event in Lithuania</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a69d497f2ff89ad160a43ce54aa20dcb88838fb2e968a6295e0caee1c6b58420</id><updated>2026-10-09T15:22:37Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T16:20:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-pulls-sponsorship-from-disinfo2026-event-in-lithuania/a-79599615--b060dac4b016.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-pulls-sponsorship-from-disinfo2026-event-in-lithuania/a-79599615?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The EU's diplomatic service, Canada and host nation Lithuania all pulled support from a disinformation event in Vilnius. Amid reports of US pressure, the EU said it was "uncomfortable with the framing" of some panels.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>How the Houthi-Saudi conflict is affecting countries on Africa's Red Sea coast — and beyond</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:230555b4266a65d954a553f4fdc81d820ee66cfcd4194026cd43626cd0c9ff7a</id><updated>2026-10-09T15:22:37Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T16:11:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-the-houthi-saudi-conflict-is-affecting-countries-on-africa-s-red-sea-coast-and-beyond/a-79588992--cc6ed789d367.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-the-houthi-saudi-conflict-is-affecting-countries-on-africa-s-red-sea-coast-and-beyond/a-79588992?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Bab el-Mandeb Strait, which Yemeni government forces are trying to take back from the Houthis, is located not far from Djibouti and other African states.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>India faces water and power shortages after weak monsoon</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:48b42d31ff1aa6a5437a33693effb8fa5603d58bbf51d6869fa82d445127a756</id><updated>2026-10-09T15:22:37Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T14:40:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-faces-water-and-power-shortages-after-weak-monsoon/a-79599540--3ab74afcb33c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-faces-water-and-power-shortages-after-weak-monsoon/a-79599540?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A weak monsoon in India is hitting farmers, water supplies and the power system, while raising wider questions about increasingly erratic rainfall and the economic costs.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>South Korea warns of AI-aided hacking after bank data breaches</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1e08a3fb00d11fab9ad6aa90f08b75eba49fe7fc571485da120a827fc50fe243</id><updated>2026-10-09T15:22:37Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T12:17:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/south-korea-warns-of-ai-aided-hacking-after-bank-data-breaches/a-79592922--3290ee11faa1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/south-korea-warns-of-ai-aided-hacking-after-bank-data-breaches/a-79592922?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Seoul is alarmed after a recent breach of South Korean banks' cyber defenses that reportedly involved AI-assisted hacking. Officials warn such methods could be used to also target other sectors and government agencies.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Security in the Black Sea region: is Bulgaria the weak link in Europe's defense against threats from Russia?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:657832c7f45be7d07cc762a216730cc3eb19ff0a106587b66d30cf23fdc2834c</id><updated>2026-10-09T15:22:37Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T11:45:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/security-in-the-black-sea-region-is-bulgaria-the-weak-link-in-europe-s-defense-against-threats-from-/a-79592663--cd93d129d2db.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/security-in-the-black-sea-region-is-bulgaria-the-weak-link-in-europe-s-defense-against-threats-from-russia/a-79592663?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Two ships have sunk off the coast of Bulgaria and Romania after drone attacks in recent days. Bulgaria has held back on pointing the finger at Russia. What does that mean for security in the Black Sea and the region?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>South Korea recalls Ukraine ambassador amid POW dispute</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bcb622bdbe181b2d0a29f9c88e54fdcf4253202cbedd033de54b5b5d3ce38660</id><updated>2026-10-09T15:22:37Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T10:55:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/south-korea-recalls-ukraine-ambassador-amid-pow-dispute/a-79590511--9732a38bcd21.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/south-korea-recalls-ukraine-ambassador-amid-pow-dispute/a-79590511?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">South Korea has said it will recall its ambassador to Ukraine. Seoul is upset about a transfer of North Korean prisoners of war being made public knowledge at the UN and had demanded — but not received — an apology.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>As Russia steps up attacks on Ukrainian data centers, could Ukraine soon be offline?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c473aca3d6b1f02c78b1ab7b225a29810287cbc4183f4b914a79347dcb8f9dbc</id><updated>2026-10-09T15:22:37Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T10:52:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/as-russia-steps-up-attacks-on-ukrainian-data-centers-could-ukraine-soon-be-offline/a-79582503--ed9380350022.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/as-russia-steps-up-attacks-on-ukrainian-data-centers-could-ukraine-soon-be-offline/a-79582503?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As Russia targets Ukraine's data centers more and more, experts say the country's internet system is too robust to shut down entirely. However, services could become more expensive.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Middle Corridor: Can Bulgaria be a safe gateway for Asian imports to the EU?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:71b50f1b56b1bfbe37fa18ab34eb97140c455d8a172974d69db0c0cf590e3840</id><updated>2026-10-09T15:22:37Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T08:38:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/middle-corridor-can-bulgaria-be-a-safe-gateway-for-asian-imports-to-the-eu/a-79584530--0deecfdaf02f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/middle-corridor-can-bulgaria-be-a-safe-gateway-for-asian-imports-to-the-eu/a-79584530?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The EU wants more trade via the Middle Corridor, which could bring big benefits for Bulgaria. But Tuesday's drone attacks on commercial ships off the Bulgarian coast are a stark reminder of the security risks involved.</summary><category term="World" /></entry></feed>
